become illumined with the smile of the geoconda. And this is where Walter Pater comes in. He's a massive, massive influence on the English-speaking world. That passage that you read, I mean, it may seem kind of, you know, purple to us. But it determines how people in the English-speaking world see the Mona Lisa for generations and generations. But the guys who really go big on this are unsurprisingly, since they own it, are the French. So I'll cite two writers in particular.
变得被焦孔多的微笑所照亮。这就是沃尔特·佩特登场的地方。他对英语世界有着巨大、巨大的影响。你读的那段话，我的意思是，对我们来说可能看起来有点华丽。但它决定了英语世界的人们几代人如何看待《蒙娜丽莎》。但真正大肆宣扬这一点的人，不出所料，因为他们拥有它，是法国人。所以我将特别引用两位作家。

