00:57:36.000 --> 00:58:16.000
Well, at least we still have the frame. The news goes around Paris, around France, around the world. Huge crowds kind of descend on the louvre. go to look at where the painting had been much larger crowds than had ever assembled when the Mona Lisa was actually in situ. And there's a desperate kind of Inspector Cluzo-type pursuit of the painting, which is always raking up ludicrous suspect. So one of them is the famous poet, Guillaume Apollinaire, who is arrested. And Apollinaire and a friend of his, who is an up-and-coming Spanish painter resident in Paris at the time called Pablo Picasso, actually end up on trial, both Apollinaire.
