the Mona Lisa had originally been painted, an antique dealer, called Alfredo Jerry gets a letter which has been signed Leonardo. And in this letter, Leonardo says that he wants to hand over the Mona Lisa to the Afizi, the great gallery in Florence, and he hints that he wants to do this for patriotic reasons. He does also say that he wants 500,000 dearer to cover his expenses, but he's going very big on the fact that he's Italian and he's doing this for patriotic reasons. So the antique dealer arranges to meet him and Leonardo, Julie arrives from Paris and Jerry and the head curator from the Ephizi asked to see the Mona Lisa. He kind of pulls the Mona Lisa out from his suitcase, unwraps it.
《蒙娜丽莎》最初是在那里绘制的，一位名叫阿尔弗雷多·杰里（Alfredo Jerry）的古董商收到了一封署名“列奥纳多”的信。在这封信中，列奥纳多说他想把《蒙娜丽莎》交给乌菲兹美术馆（Afizi），即佛罗伦萨的伟大画廊，他暗示他想出于爱国原因这样做。他也确实说他想要50万第纳尔来支付他的费用，但他非常强调他是意大利人，他这样做是出于爱国原因。所以古董商安排见他，列奥纳多·朱利（Leonardo Julie）从巴黎赶来，杰里和乌菲兹美术馆的首席馆长要求看《蒙娜丽莎》。他从手提箱里拿出《蒙娜丽莎》，拆开包装。

