The head curator of the Ephizzi inspects it. It's clear it is indeed the Mona Lisa. And so they have the thief arrested. And he turns out to be a guy called Vincenzo Perugia. And he was an Italian painter-decorator who had been working in the Louvre, painting the walls on the Fateful Monday that the painting was stolen. And he seized his chance. And he just lifted it out from his frame, hidden it under his coat, walked off across the courtyard of the Louvre. He kind of waved at a guard and gone out through the door.
乌菲兹美术馆的首席馆长检查了它。很明显，它确实是《蒙娜丽莎》。于是他们逮捕了小偷。他原来是一个名叫文森佐·佩鲁贾（Vincenzo Perugia）的人。他是一位意大利油漆工兼装饰工，在那个命运攸关的星期一，他一直在卢浮宫工作，粉刷墙壁。他抓住了机会。他只是把它从画框里取出来，藏在外套下，走过卢浮宫的庭院。他向守卫挥了挥手，从门口走了出去。

